# learned-model-service.form - a learned model served over HTTP, from shared parts

(learned-model-service
  (lineage
    (rests-on http-server.bml affine-train.fk channel.fk cell-sync-transport.form)
    (model-handler form/form-stdlib/model-service.fk)
    (middleware form/form-stdlib/http-layer.fk)
    (assembly form/form-stdlib/presence-service.fk)
    (proof-core form/form-stdlib/tests/model-serve-core-band.fk -> 15)
    (proof-handler form/form-stdlib/tests/model-handler-band.fk -> 7)
    (proof-service form/form-stdlib/tests/model-service-band.fk -> 255)
    (proof-wire form/form-stdlib/tests/presence-service-band.fk -> 127))

  (purpose
    "A LEARNED model served over the HTTP verb surface, assembled from parts each cell can build and share independently."
    "Each part is its own recipe + proof band: a model-backed handler (the ML part), a middleware layer (the 'anyone can add a layer' part), and an assembly that composes them with the data-driven router. The model is DATA — train it on one presence, share the weights, serve the same predictions on another."
    "Anyone can add a part: a new route, a new handler, a new middleware layer, or a new trained model is one recipe/one row, picked up by a running presence without restart.")

  (parts
    (verb-router "http-server.bml + kernel-http.fk: data-driven dispatch — routes are kh-route DATA, handlers a named registry. Adding a route is adding a row, never editing the flow.")
    (model-handler "model-service.fk: ms-predict runs the learned affine model (weights = (list w b), scale 1000, from affine-train.fk's SGD); ms-predict-handler is a FACTORY that returns a handler closure bound to a presence's own weights; ms-body renders the prediction as JSON.")
    (middleware "http-layer.fk: layer-wrap turns (handler, layer-fn) into a handler; layer-stamp adds a provenance header; layer-gate is an auth gate (401 without the key); layer-stack folds a LIST of layers so adding one is appending a row.")
    (assembly "presence-service.fk: psvc-serve composes router + model handler + chosen layers into one served service; the model and the layers are PARAMETERS each presence supplies."))

  (floor
    "Every band answers in full on ./fkwu: model-serve-core-band 15 (the learned inference as data and the JSON render), model-handler-band 7 (the factory closure that captures the learned weights serves their prediction), model-service-band 255 (the model-backed handler closure with stamp + gate middleware, at the value level), and presence-service-band 127 (the full HTTP wire: 200 OK with the prediction, model-as-data swap 6000 vs 9000, stamp header, gate 401-without / serve-with, a second route, oracle-tied body)."
    "Closures that capture data and closures that call other closures both carry on fkwu: the whole middleware composition runs on the body's own kernel.")

  (north-star
    "Presences run a real service mesh: a model trained on one host is gossiped over a channel, picked up by peers, served per host (native-first where the recipe lowers, kernel-walked otherwise), and offered onward. A new layer (auth, rate-limit, translation) authored by anyone composes into every presence's stack by appending one row."
    "The HTTP verb surface is the example; the same shape carries any BML recipe — a learned classifier, a translation lens, a compute kernel — built as a part, shared as a node, integrated live.")

  (receipt-command
    (core    "./fkwu form/form-stdlib/tests/model-serve-core-band.fk")
    (handler "./fkwu form/form-stdlib/tests/model-handler-band.fk")
    (service "./fkwu form/form-stdlib/tests/model-service-band.fk")
    (wire    "./fkwu form/form-stdlib/tests/presence-service-band.fk"))

  (open
    (socket "psvc-serve takes a raw HTTP/1.1 STRING and returns a response STRING. The kernel carries socket_listen / socket_accept / socket_send / socket_recv (router-proof-io.bml uses them); binding psvc-serve to a live socket is the next seam.")
    (federation "A model crosses presences as a frozen node over a channel: one presence learns and freezes it, another reads the same node and serves it. Running that exchange live between two presences on this Mac, then across the fleet, is the witness still to take.")
    (live-serve-is-kernel-walk "A running presence serves rich recipes by walking them on the kernel; the affine subset lowers native, HTTP/ML do not lower yet. Native-first when ready, walk otherwise.")
    (shared-vocabulary-deps "A shared model crosses as DATA; the predict/render recipe must already exist in the receiver (the shared stdlib vocabulary). A recipe that calls an unknown function needs that dependency shipped or registry-resolved — named in cell-sync-transport.form.")))
